{
  "//": "KaTeX is a stylesheet-only dependency here. Keep its release identical to the markup producer, rehype-katex 7.0.1 (declares ^0.16.0); micromark-extension-math 3.1.0 also declares ^0.16.0. BST-2031 tested CSS 0.19.0 against the real lockfile: scripts/__tests__/katex-css-renderer-parity.test.mjs rejects the 0.19/0.16 split. KaTeX 0.18 renamed internal classes, so updating CSS alone breaks rendering. Retain the matched 0.16.47 pair until its owners admit a patched release; GHSA-238p-pmpm-9mq7 remains a documented low-severity residual (patched floor 0.18.2). Mermaid 12 has its own compatible ^0.18.0 renderer; the Mermaid CLI still separately declares ^0.16.25. These are distinct owner paths, not permission for a global cross-range override. No source imports KaTeX JavaScript directly; the parity guard enforces that premise.",
